---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Shipping Policy',
  description: 'Shipping and delivery policy of shengyuanpeptides.com — packaging, dispatch times, carriers, tracking, customs, and loss handling.',
};

---

<BaseLayout
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  title="Shipping Policy | Shengyuan Peptide"
  description="How Shandong Shengyuan Peptide ships research peptides: cold-chain packaging, dispatch times, international express carriers, tracking, customs responsibilities, and loss handling."
>
  <div class="wrap article-shell">
    <div class="article-header">
      <h1>Shipping Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">How we pack, ship, and track your research peptides worldwide.</p>
    </div>
    <article>
      <h2>Packaging</h2>
      <p>
        Peptides are lyophilized and sealed in sterile vials, then packed with cold-chain protection —
        insulated packaging with temperature buffers where needed — so that products remain stable
        during transit. Oxidation-sensitive peptides are packaged under inert atmosphere in amber
        vials. Each parcel ships with its batch Certificate of Analysis.
      </p>

      <h2>Dispatch Times</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Stock catalog items</th><td>Ship within 24–48 hours of order confirmation</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Custom synthesis</th><td>Ships after QC release; typically 10–20 business days from kick-off</td></tr>
          <tr><th>OEM programs</th><td>Timeline agreed in the project plan</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Carriers and Tracking</h2>
      <p>
        We ship through international express networks (FedEx, DHL, UPS, and equivalents) to 50+
        countries. A tracking number is emailed the moment your parcel leaves our facility, and
        transit typically takes 3–7 business days depending on destination. Estimates are not
        guaranteed delivery dates; customs handling times are outside our control.
      </p>

      <h2>Address Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for providing a complete and accurate recipient name, address, phone
        number, and postal code. If a parcel is not delivered because of an error in the address you
        provided, no reshipment is provided. If you discover an error after confirming an order,
        contact us immediately with your order reference.
      </p>

      <h2>Customs and Import</h2>
      <p>
        The buyer is responsible for confirming that the ordered materials may lawfully be imported
        into the destination country and for any duties, taxes, or clearance requirements. We provide
        documentation support (COA, commercial invoice) with every shipment. A product's availability
        for shipment does not constitute advice that it may lawfully be imported into a particular
        destination.
      </p>

      <h2>Damaged Shipments</h2>
      <p>
        Report any damage within 48 hours of receipt with photographs; we will investigate and arrange
        replacement of affected items. Photographs and an unboxing video are recommended so the issue
        can be assessed quickly.
      </p>

      <h2>Lost Shipments</h2>
      <p>
        Lost shipments are re-sent once the carrier confirms non-delivery. We monitor tracking on
        confirmed orders; you do not need to submit a separate claim when we have already identified
        the issue.
      </p>

      <h2>Customs Returns and Reshipment</h2>
      <p>
        Where a parcel is returned by customs or the carrier, we coordinate reshipment or a
        resolution with the buyer individually. Each case is reviewed on its tracking record,
        destination, and circumstances.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about shipping: <a href="mailto:aaron@shengyuanpeptides.com">aaron@shengyuanpeptides.com</a>
        or WhatsApp +64 2102668969.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
